Clear the mapping arrays when sctp_process_init() resets the peer's initial TSN.

sctp_process_init() sets mapping_array_base_tsn, cumulative_tsn and the
highest-TSN markers from the INIT's initial TSN but leaves mapping_array and
nr_mapping_array as they are. A new association starts with zeroed arrays and
the restart path (case A) clears them first, but a COOKIE-ECHO handled as case B
of RFC 9260 section 5.2.4 (our tag matches, peer tag differs) on an established
association that already received DATA keeps the old bits. They then mark TSNs
of the new sequence space as received, and the next sctp_slide_mapping_arrays()
computes a cumulative TSN above the highest TSN: INVARIANTS panic "cumack
greater than high-tsn" (reached via sctp_sack_check after DATA).

Includes programs/test_cookie_case_b.c: it plays the peer of a connecting
socket over AF_CONN, keeps the cookie of the INIT-ACK sent for a colliding
INIT, establishes the association with another peer tag/TSN, sends one DATA
chunk, then echoes the kept cookie (case B) and sends the first DATA chunk of
the new TSN space. Without the fix that chunk is dropped as a duplicate (the
test fails) and with INVARIANTS the process aborts in
sctp_slide_mapping_arrays().

Upstream: none found.

